    "body": "Review fix pushed (head 85b2d478, a merge of current main plus one docs commit). `Fixes #1261` is kept, because the page now covers what the issue asks for:\n\n1. Common refusals per kind: each section (Mill, Lathe, Mill-turn, Plasma) now has a \"Common refusals\" line. The lines quote refusal strings that exist on main: `posting_family.rs` (family door and wire EDM post), `machine/judge.rs` (tilt, rotary travel), `lathe_voice.rs` (off-axis Drill), `setup_workholding.rs` (G97 and C-axis workholding maximum), `machine/lathe_stroke.rs`, `posting_serves.rs` (#1265: does not serve, not a turning post), `machine/plasma.rs` and `crates/post/src/machine/plasma.rs`. Placeholders are shown as `<kind>` etc. inside code spans.\n2. EDM status: the section now says that Wire Contour can be created and generated on a user-written `wire_edm` machine file, that posting it is refused by name (\"posts through a wire EDM post, which is not built yet - nothing is posted\"), and that sinker EDM admits no operation yet.\n3. Note: #1265 has merged, so its \"in review\" sentence is replaced with the behaviour now on main. PR body updated to match.\n\nGate: `zola build` and `zola check --skip-external-links` from `site/` pass. Flagging ready.",
